W: 1. Will ye go to Flanders, my Mally-O?
W: Will ye go to Flanders, bonny Mally-O?
W: There ye'll have sack and brandy and cake and sugar candy,
W: Will ye go to Flanders, my Mally-O?
W:
W: 2. Will ye go to Flanders, my Mally-O?
W: Along wi' a' the Hielanders, Bonnie, Mally-O
W: You'll hear the captain calling, you'll see the sergeant crawling,
W: And the soldiers, how they're falling, my Mally-O.
W:
W: 3. Will ye go to Flanders, my Mally-O?
W: To see the chief commanders, my bonny Mally-O?
W: You'll see the bullets fly, and the ladies how they cry,
W: And the soldiers how they die, my Mally, O.
